## JWT Structure

```
eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyNDIiLCJyb2xlcyI6WyJVU0VSIl0sImlhdCI6MTcwMDAwMDAwMCwiZXhwIjoxNzAwMDAzNjAwfQ.SflKxwRJSMeKKF2QT4fwpMeJf36POk6yJV_adQssw5c

Part 1 (Header):
  Base64URL decode → {"alg": "HS256", "typ": "JWT"}

Part 2 (Payload):
  Base64URL decode → {
    "sub": "user42",
    "roles": ["USER"],
    "iat": 1700000000,  // issued at
    "exp": 1700003600   // expires at (1 hour later)
  }
  !!! Anyone can read this — Base64 is not encryption !!!

Part 3 (Signature):
  HMAC-SHA256(base64url(header) + '.' + base64url(payload), secretKey)
  → tamper-evident: modify any byte → signature won't match
```

